<title>HUNGARY: Hungary two-year bond yield drops to 18.61 pct.</title>
<headline>Hungary two-year bond yield drops to 18.61 pct.</headline>
<dateline>BUDAPEST 1997-03-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>The average annual yield on the latest issue of Hungary's two-year government bonds was set by auction at 18.61 percent, down from 18.62 percent at an auction on February 27, the Government Debt Management Agency said on Thursday.</p>
<p>    BONDS OF THE 1999/F SERIES</p>
<p>    Date of issue		 4 March 1997</p>
<p>    Date of maturity	   4 December 1999</p>
<p>    Total on offer	    10,000 million forints</p>
<p>    Total bids received     26,656.52 million forints</p>
<p>    Total allocated	   10,000 million forints</p>
<p>    Total issued		11,000 million forints</p>
<p>    Average annual yield	  18.61 pct</p>
<p>    Average price		   97.70 pct</p>
<p>NOTE: The bond bears a fixed interest rate of 16.5 percent, payable semi- anually starting from October 12, 1997.</p>
<p>-- Budapest newsroom +36 1 327 4040</p>
